---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';

const pubDate = new Date('2026-01-18');
---

<Layout
	title="BMS Research & AI Survey"
	description="Help us understand Burning Mouth Syndrome better through data and AI research."
	pubDate={pubDate}
>
	<div class="research-page">
		<p>Burning Mouth Syndrome remains a mystery to much of the medical world. My goal is to use data and modern AI to uncover patterns that could lead to better management and eventually a cure.</p>
		
		<div style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1); padding: 2.5rem; border-radius: 20px; margin: 3rem 0; text-align: center;">
			<h3 style="color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 1rem;">The BMS Patient Survey</h3>
			<p>I am developing a comprehensive survey to gather detailed data on symptoms, triggers, and relief methods from patients worldwide.</p>
			
			<div style="margin-top: 2rem;">
				<p><strong>Interested in participating?</strong></p>
				<p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 2rem;">Join the waitlist to be notified when the survey goes live and contribute your experience to the research.</p>
				
				<form style="max-width: 400px; margin: 0 auto; display: flex; gap: 0.5rem;">
					<input type="email" placeholder="Your email address" required style="flex-grow: 1; padding: 0.8rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1); background: rgba(0,0,0,0.2); color: white;" />
					<button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary" style="padding: 0.8rem 1.5rem;">Notify Me</button>
				</form>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2>Why AI Research?</h2>
		<p>BMS symptoms are often subjective and vary wildly between patients. AI is uniquely suited to processing large amounts of "noisy" data to find clusters—groups of patients who share similar triggers or responses to certain treatments.</p>
		
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Pattern Recognition</strong>: Identifying common dietary or lifestyle triggers.</li>
			<li><strong>Treatment Efficacy</strong>: Seeing what actually works for specific types of BMS.</li>
			<li><strong>Data-Driven Advocacy</strong>: Using hard numbers to show the medical community the impact of this condition.</li>
		</ul>

		<p>All data collected will be anonymized and used strictly for research purposes to benefit the BMS community.</p>
	</div>
</Layout>
